■ JCROSS_FRAG_86064665
【状態】 確定
【主体】 Under Fair Credit Reporting Act FCRA consumer
【関係】 claims in
【客体】 good faith he she has been victim of fraud-related crime nationwide consumer reporting agency must include fraud alert on consumer's credit report for at least 12 months

[L2_Archive]
Under the Fair Credit Reporting Act (FCRA), if a consumer claims in good faith that he or she has been a victim of a fraud-related crime, a nationwide consumer reporting agency must include a fraud alert on the consumer's credit report for at least 12 months.

