【客体】 notice is placed on consumer's credit report to alert creditors other organizations consumer may be victim of identity theft fraud

[L2_Archive]
A fraud alert is a notice that is placed on a consumer's credit report to alert creditors and other organizations that the consumer may be a victim of identity theft or fraud.

